I have a fix for the bug in wanderer.  (You know, the one where you get
killed by a falling boulder when you are not under its flight path, but the
@ in someone's e-mail address is :-).  I would note that this bug was
present at least as far back as version 2.0.  Back then, It only happened
on screen 11, but that was probably because there were only 20 screens.  It
was still possible to solve screen 11, which might explain why the bug has
not seen much attention until now.

Try this on for size.  I have not tested it thoroughly, but I am satisfied
with it:

*** fall.c.dist	Thu May 24 18:47:13 1990
--- fall.c	Wed Jun 20 16:13:59 1990
***************
*** 143,149
      retval+=fall(mx,my,nx ,y+1,sx,sy,howdead);
      moving = 0;
      retval+=check(mx,my,x,y-1,0,1,sx,sy,howdead);
!     if(screen[y+1][nx] == '@')
          {
      	strcpy(howdead,"a falling boulder");
      	return(1);
--- 143,149 -----
      retval+=fall(mx,my,nx ,y+1,sx,sy,howdead);
      moving = 0;
      retval+=check(mx,my,x,y-1,0,1,sx,sy,howdead);
!     if((screen[y+1][nx] == '@') && ((y+1) < NOOFROWS))
